            <div xml:id="d874">

                <pb facs="0855" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.5914/187a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Egan </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-06T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 6, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. Please obtain and mail at the very earliest opportunity an official map
                    showing specifically the boundaries of the group of islands, keys and rocks in
                    the West Indies over which Denmark claims sovereignty and which she cedes to the
                    United States under the pending treaty. This map should be the official
                    expression of the Government of Denmark as to the geographic limits of the
                    Danish West Indies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
